libfprint-egis0576 (1:1.94.100-99egis1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Rebuild of upstream libfprint v1.94.100 with the out-of-tree egis0576
    (EgisTec EH576, USB 1c7a:0576) driver compiled in. Mirrors
    packaging/fedora/libfprint.spec: same upstream version, same meson
    integration patch, same suspend/resume sleep hook and udev rule.
  * Epoch "1:" added. Debian trixie's stock libfprint-2-2 is 1:1.94.9-1 and
    sid/forky's is 1:1.94.10-1. An epoch always outranks the upstream
    version and the revision below it, so a build with no epoch sorts
    below both of those even though its own upstream version (1.94.100) is
    higher. Carrying the same epoch "1:" fixes that:
      dpkg --compare-versions '1:1.94.100-99egis1' gt '1:1.94.9-1'   -> true
      dpkg --compare-versions '1:1.94.100-99egis1' gt '1:1.94.10-1'  -> true
    The "-99egis1" revision then does the same job the Fedora spec's
    Release: 99...egis9 does within one upstream Version: the numeric 99
    sorts above any plausible normal Debian revision (-1, -2, ...) at the
    same epoch and upstream Version, including a hypothetical future
    Debian rebuild of 1.94.100 itself:
      dpkg --compare-versions '1:1.94.100-99egis1' gt '1:1.94.100-1'  -> true
    No Provides, Conflicts or Replaces is needed as a result, and no
    install-time flag is needed either.

